      "summary": "The delivery policy, replay checks, and in-memory commit behavior appear to meet the stated outcomes. The no-dispatch test has a blind spot for external sends from async API helpers.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/MockRequestDeliveryTests.cs",
          "line": 382,
          "message": "The transitive call-graph test misses sends in API async state machines. Include generated MoveNext methods in the walk or reject async API methods so the test fails if an async external-send path is added.",
          "confidence": 0.88,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The call graph follows method tokens in API method bodies, but it does not inspect compiler-generated async state-machine MoveNext methods. An API async helper calls framework AsyncTaskMethodBuilder.Start, which is allowed and is not traversed.",
            "failureScenario": "If Submit calls an API async helper that sends through HttpClient from its generated MoveNext method, the walk can stop at the allowed framework Start call and pass without seeing the send. This leaves the no-dispatch acceptance criterion unguarded for that reachable path."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
