      },
      "summary": "The delivery behavior tests cover the stated eligibility, rejection, replay, conflict, concurrency, atomicity, correction, and wording cases. The no-dispatch check has a gap: its tests do not ensure the call-graph traversal continues to enforce the unresolved-dispatch guard.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/MockRequestDeliveryTests.cs",
          "line": 323,
          "message": "The no-dispatch tests check the unresolved-dispatch helper in isolation, so they do not fail if its enforcement is removed from the transitive call-graph walk.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The guard test checks IsUnresolvedApiDispatch directly, while the delivery call-graph test separately invokes that helper during traversal. It never verifies that the traversal still enforces the check.",
            "failureScenario": "If the Assert.False(IsUnresolvedApiDispatch(...)) guard is removed from the call-graph walk, the helper assertions still pass. The suite can then pass even if delivery adds unresolved interface or virtual dispatch, contrary to the criterion requiring the no-dispatch checks to be enforced."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
